WEBVTT

NOTE threshold-questions: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.571
Why the table and the
push dialog disagree,

V0-2
00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:08.230
and what the second option really does.

V1a-1
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:20.022
Station 11AP2 suggests 6 percent.
With a 10 percent threshold set,

V1a-2
00:00:20.122 --> 00:00:24.090
the table still shows 6,
and it always will.

V1b-1
00:00:24.653 --> 00:00:27.828
The threshold is applied only
in the Push Changes dialog,

V1b-2
00:00:27.928 --> 00:00:30.603
and to what is sent to
Lynx. Never to the table.

V2a-1
00:00:38.673 --> 00:00:43.421
Open Push Changes and the same station
shows its original value and the rewritten

V2a-2
00:00:43.521 --> 00:00:47.683
one side by side, with the banner
counting how many rows were affected.

V2b-1
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.720
This is the disagreement,
and it is intentional.

V3a-1
00:00:58.603 --> 00:01:02.303
Set to zero skips the station:
Lynx receives 0 percent.

V3a-2
00:01:02.403 --> 00:01:07.516
Set to the minimum threshold value lifts
the suggestion up to the threshold,

V3a-3
00:01:07.616 --> 00:01:10.173
so the station still gets a short run.

V3b-1
00:01:10.687 --> 00:01:12.967
They are opposite behaviours
from the same number.

V4a-1
00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:24.463
Exclude Zeros is available only under
the second option. A station whose

V4a-2
00:01:24.563 --> 00:01:29.430
suggestion is a true zero stays at zero,
instead of being lifted to the threshold.

V4b-1
00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.750
Without it, a station that needs
no water gets a small run anyway.

V5a-1
00:01:40.387 --> 00:01:42.803
A threshold of zero turns
the whole thing off,

V5a-2
00:01:42.903 --> 00:01:45.057
and the option group is disabled with it.

V5b-1
00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.596
If the push dialog shows no
banner, check this first.

V5b-2
00:01:48.696 --> 00:01:52.290
The setting is site-level, and
someone else may have cleared it.
